## LAPACK is called from C in ibic_score.c and ibge_score.c (dpotrf, dtrtrs),
## so the package must link R's LAPACK and BLAS. $(LAPACK_LIBS),
## $(BLAS_LIBS) and $(FLIBS) come from R's etc/Makeconf.
##
## WHY THIS MATTERS, and why the file is a .in with a configure script.
##
## This file used to exist WITHOUT a configure script, which meant R never
## read it: nothing substituted it into src/Makevars, so PKG_LIBS was never
## applied and dpotrf_/dtrtrs_ were left as undefined symbols in idlBNs.so,
## to be resolved from whatever happened to be loaded in the process. On
## macOS that turned out to be Apple's Accelerate framework -- confirmed
## with dladdr() -- and not R's own libRlapack, even though R itself uses
## libRlapack. The two do not agree: over 400 random Cholesky
## factorisations they differed in 365, by up to 8.9e-16 per element. So the
## package's arithmetic silently depended on the platform.
##
## Linking explicitly fixes that. The compiled code now uses whichever
## LAPACK R itself was built against, so results depend on R's own
## configuration rather than on load order.
##
## Writing R Extensions asks for $(BLAS_LIBS) to be followed by $(FLIBS),
## and R CMD check enforces that textually on this file, so the reference
## below is spelled out literally.
##
## But $(FLIBS) names a gfortran runtime at the exact path R was built
## against, and that tree is absent on some machines that can otherwise
## build this package perfectly well. configure therefore tests whether it
## links, and drops it from the generated src/Makevars if it does not.
##
## Dropping it is safe HERE specifically: there are no Fortran sources, and
## R's libRlapack already links libgfortran and libquadmath itself, so the
## Fortran runtime is satisfied transitively. It changes nothing about WHICH
## LAPACK is used, only whether the runtime is named again on the link line.
##
## Note that overriding FLIBS to empty in a Makevars does NOT work: R passes
## it to make on the command line, and command-line assignments beat
## makefile ones. The reference has to be removed, not neutralised.
PKG_LIBS = $(LAPACK_LIBS) $(BLAS_LIBS) $(FLIBS)
